comments.content:
Global `outline: none` on every focusable element removes the only visible focus indicator, and only a short whitelist of selectors (`.ask-user__opt`, `.modal-actions .btn`, `.settings-page :is(...)`, `[data-slot="button|input|select-trigger"]`, `.sidebar-footer-action`, draggable tree rows) re-adds one. Any interactive element outside that list — plain `.menu-panel`/`.search-panel__row` rows, `.tree-l3`, `.tree-icon-btn`, chips, custom `<div role="button">` controls — is keyboard-invisible. Prefer suppressing only mouse focus while keeping a default visible ring:
```css
:focus:not(:focus-visible) {
  outline: none;
}
```
and audit the remaining elements so each has an explicit `:focus-visible` style.

