comments.content:
Fixed sleep to wait for process-tree termination: on a loaded CI box 800ms may not be enough for the child (and its descendants) to be reaped, and on an idle box it wastes time. Prefer polling with a deadline so the assertion is both faster and more robust, e.g.:
```rust
let deadline = tokio::time::Instant::now() + Duration::from_secs(5);
while sentinel.exists() && tokio::time::Instant::now() < deadline {
    tokio::time::sleep(Duration::from_millis(20)).await;
}
